              <h2 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-0.3px;line-height:1.3;color:#232F3E;">Run the framework yourself</h2>

              <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;">Applying it to a shortlist takes four steps:</p>

              <ol style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 0 24px;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;">
                <li style="margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:6px;">List the 25 criteria down a spreadsheet with the weights (they sum to 100%): one row per criterion, one column per vendor.</li>
                <li style="margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:6px;">Score each vendor 0&ndash;5 per criterion from public sources &mdash; API reference, benchmark, security page &mdash; and record the evidence tier. Mark anything you cannot evidence as NOT-FOUND and score it conservatively.</li>
                <li style="margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:6px;">Compute both numbers: the composite (weighted sum) and the risk-adjusted score (apply the penalty rules; floor at 0.00).</li>
                <li style="margin:0;padding-left:6px;">Read the <em>gap</em> between the two numbers. A small gap means the weaknesses are spread thin. A large gap means a disqualifying hole &mdash; investigate that hole before anything else.</li>
              </ol>

              <p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;"><em>Prefer not to build this from scratch? The <a href="https://newsletter.ionova.ai/iso-20022-vendor-workbook?utm_source=newsletter" style="color:#0972D3;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;">ISO 20022 Address Vendor Scoring Workbook</a> has it pre-loaded.</em></p>

              <!-- PULL QUOTE -->
              <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin:0 0 20px;">
                <tr>
                  <td style="background:#F5F9FF;border:1px solid #D0DAEB;border-left:3px solid #43ADC1;border-radius:4px;padding:16px 20px;">
                    <p style="margin:0;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-style:italic;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#466587;">A framework you can run against us is a framework you can trust when you run it against anyone.</p>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>

              <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;">The framework is applied end-to-end, criterion by criterion, on <a href="https://www.ionova.ai/compare?utm_source=newsletter" style="color:#0972D3;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;">the comparison pages</a> &mdash; including ioNova vs the <a href="https://www.ionova.ai/compare/swift-ai-address-model?utm_source=newsletter" style="color:#0972D3;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;">SWIFT AI Parser</a>, vs <a href="https://www.ionova.ai/compare/loqate?utm_source=newsletter" style="color:#0972D3;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;">Loqate (GBG)</a>, vs <a href="https://www.ionova.ai/compare/smarty?utm_source=newsletter" style="color:#0972D3;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;">Smarty</a>, vs <a href="https://www.ionova.ai/compare/melissa?utm_source=newsletter" style="color:#0972D3;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;">Melissa</a>, vs <a href="https://www.ionova.ai/compare/geopostcodes?utm_source=newsletter" style="color:#0972D3;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;">GeoPostCodes</a>, vs <a href="https://www.ionova.ai/compare/structx?utm_source=newsletter" style="color:#0972D3;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;">StructX</a>, and vs <a href="https://www.ionova.ai/compare/catalyst-di?utm_source=newsletter" style="color:#0972D3;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;">Catalyst DI</a>.</p>

              <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;">Thirty years of building payments and screening systems has taught me that under a deadline, capability and delivery are two different questions, and you have to ask both. It is the same instinct that made us build an engine to <em>resolve and fix, not validate and block</em> &mdash; to repair the address and preserve the identifier, rather than reject the payment and hand you an exception. Show your work, and let the buyer check it.</p>

              <p style="margin:0;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#232F3E;">So run the framework. Run it on every vendor on your desk. <strong>Then run it on us.</strong></p>
            </td>
          </tr>

          <!-- SECTION: your next step -->
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:32px 36px;border-bottom:1px solid #E8E8E8;">
